To call an API with a token via Postman, follow these steps:

1. Open Postman

Launch Postman on your system.

2. Select HTTP Method

Choose GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, or any other method as per API requirements.

Enter the API URL in the request bar.


3. Add Authorization Token

Option 1: Using Authorization Tab (Recommended)

1. Go to the Authorization tab.


2. Select Bearer Token in the Type dropdown.


3. Paste your token in the Token field.



Option 2: Using Headers (Alternative)

1. Go to the Headers tab.


2. Add a new key: Authorization


3. Set the value as:

Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE



4. Add Request Body (For POST, PUT)

If your API requires data, go to the Body tab.

Select raw and choose JSON as the format.

Enter the request payload in JSON format, e.g.:

{
  "name": "Pankaj",
  "email": "pankaj@example.com"
}


5. Send Request

Click Send and check the response.

