Step 3: Check API Authentication Setup in ASP.NET Core

If you are using ASP.NET Core, check your authentication configuration:

🔹 Ensure Authentication Middleware is Configured

In Program.cs or Startup.cs, make sure authentication is added:

builder.Services.AddAuthentication(JwtBearerDefaults.AuthenticationScheme)
    .AddJwtBearer(options =>
    {
        options.Authority = "https://your-auth-server.com";
        options.Audience = "your-api-resource";
    });

🔹 Verify Claims Extraction

In your API controller, try logging claims:

[Authorize]
[HttpGet("test")]
public IActionResult Test()
{
    var user = HttpContext.User;
    if (!user.Identity.IsAuthenticated)
    {
        return Unauthorized("User is not authenticated");
    }

    var claims = user.Claims.Select(c => new { c.Type, c.Value }).ToList();
    return Ok(claims);
}

If user.Claims is empty, the token is either invalid or not containing claims.



